{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The controls move parts of a coloured arm; there’s no freely moving avatar. On clones, four buttons extend successive sections right, up, right, and down by three pixels. The tip and target share the pink colour, but walls lie between them. I’ll test retraction and collision limits before planning a route."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > probe_level2.py <<'PY'\nimport gkm_try\nfrom legs import align_marked_bar_tips\nfrom perception import arr, safe_step\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef sig(e):\n a=arr(e.frame()); out=[]\n for col in (12,10,11,14):\n  yy,xx=np.where((a==col)&(np.indices(a.shape)[0]<54));out.append((col, (int(xx.min()),int(yy.min()),int(xx.max()),int(yy.max()))))\n yy,xx=np.where((a==13)&(np.indices(a.shape)[0]<54));out.append(('pink',list(zip(xx.tolist(),yy.tolist()))));return out\n\ndef probe(env):\n align_marked_bar_tips(env);c=env.clone();a=arr(c.frame())\n print('WALL ROWS')\n for y in range(64):\n  xs=np.where(a[y]==15)[0]\n  if len(xs) and (y==0 or not np.array_equal(xs,np.where(a[y-1]==15)[0])):print(y,xs.tolist())\n for x in (12,27,42,57):\n  cc=c.clone(); states=[]\n  for i in range(20):\n   prev=arr(cc.frame()).copy();safe_step(cc,(6,x,57))\n   if np.array_equal(prev,arr(cc.frame())):break\n   states.append(sig(cc))\n  print('EXTEND',x,'steps',len(states),'last',states[-1] if states else None)\n  if states:\n   safe_step(cc,(6,x-6,57));print('RETRACT',x,sig(cc))\n cc=c.clone();align_marked_bar_tips(cc);print('OLD_LEG',cc.levels_completed,sig(cc))\n\ngkm_try.A.run_program('s5i5',probe)\nPY\npython probe_level2.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
